    "probe_text": "This is the V1 controller's `addOwner` method (lines 189\u2013319), which backs `POST /api/owners`. Here is every validation and side-effect, in the exact order they execute.\n\n## Pre-entry\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the method never runs.\n\n## Required-field validation (lines 190\u2013211)\n2. **Address normalization (side-effect, runs first)** \u2014 the raw address is normalized *before* the presence check: trimmed, internal whitespace collapsed, upper-cased, and street-type abbreviations expanded (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). `null` becomes `\"\"`.\n3. **Presence checks** \u2014 collect into a list any of these that are blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, the **normalized** `address`, `city`, `telephone`. If the list is non-empty, throw `InvalidRequestException` \u2192 **400** (all missing fields reported together).\n\n## Mapping + field normalization/validation (lines 212\u2013223)\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n5. **Store normalized address** \u2014 sets the address computed in step 2.\n6. **Telephone normalization + validation** \u2014 strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep the `+` country code if present, else assume default `+61` and drop a single leading `0`. Must match E.164 (`+` then 8\u201315 digits) or **400**. For known country codes it also enforces a fixed national-number length (`+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210) or **400**. The E.164 result is stored.\n7. **Email normalization + validation (optional)** \u2014 blank/absent \u2192 stored as `null`. Otherwise must match the email regex or **400**; lower-cased; if the domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**. Lower-cased value stored.\n8. **Postcode validation (optional)** \u2014 blank/absent passes. If present, must be exactly 4 digits or **400**; and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), the postcode must fall in that region's range (2000\u20132099 / 3000\u20133099 / 4000\u20134099) or **400**. Value is stored as-supplied (not modified).\n\n## Registration date (lines 226\u2013237)\n9. **Future-date validation** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400** (checked against the raw supplied value).\n10. **Default (side-effect)** \u2014 if none supplied, set to the server's current date.\n11. **Business-day roll (side-effect)** \u2014 if the effective date lands on Saturday/Sunday, roll forward to the next Monday. All date-derived values below use this adjusted date.\n\n## Limit / capacity checks (lines 240\u2013250)\n12. **Count owners registered on that date** (read).\n13. **Daily-limit validation** \u2014 if that count \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n14. **Bulk-signup warning (side-effect)** \u2014 set `bulkSignupWarning = (count > 80)`.\n15. **City-capacity validation** \u2014 if existing owners in the owner's city \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityCapacityException`.\n\n## Household + duplicate detection (lines 257\u2013299)\n16. **Household ID (side-effect)** \u2014 set `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of `<normalizedLastName>|<postcode>`.\n17. **Household-duplicate validation** \u2014 if any existing owner already carries this `householdId`: if the request set `sharesHousehold=true`, mark it a declared household member; otherwise throw `DuplicateHouseholdException` \u2192 **409**.\n18. **Identity-key collision validation** \u2014 compute the identity key (`<telephone>|<email>|<householdId>`); if it exactly matches an existing owner's \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n19. **Soft-match / possible-duplicate flagging (side-effect)** \u2014 unless a declared household member, look for an existing owner with the same last name + postcode but a *different* telephone (lowest id wins). Set `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` accordingly (or `possibleDuplicate=false`).\n\n## Derived fields (lines 302\u2013307)\n20. **Namesake count (side-effect)** \u2014 set `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive).\n21. **Customer code (side-effect)** \u2014 set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode range, else city table, else `UNKNOWN`; hash of telephone+lastName).\n22. **Membership number (side-effect)** \u2014 set `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (last two digits of the registration year).\n\n## Persist + respond (lines 308\u2013318)\n23. **Persist (side-effect)** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n24. **Household size read-back (side-effect)** \u2014 `populateHouseholdSize` sets `householdSize` = count of owners sharing the `householdId` (including this one).\n25. **Map to `OwnerDto`.**\n26. **Audit log (side-effect)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and membershipLevel.\n27. **Location header (side-effect)** \u2014 set to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n28. **Return 201 Created** with the owner DTO.\n\n**Note on ordering:** validations are not all front-loaded \u2014 telephone/email/postcode/date validations and several persistent side-effects (household id, namesake count, customer code) are interleaved, and the two `409` duplicate checks run *after* the `400` field validations and the limit/capacity checks. So a single request can mutate derived state and hit a later `400`/`409`; nothing is persisted until step 23, but the exception thrown depends on this order."
